From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weegee <748975+Weegee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:41:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drv: no recovery work after remove, survive an oversized set
 file

remove and shutdown stop the firmware in the teardown. If the firmware
is hung, that stop command times out and fthd_hw_hung() queues
recover_work. Nothing cancelled it again before dev_priv was freed, so
the work later ran on freed memory. Cancel it after the teardown.

Between the teardown and fthd_v4l2_unregister() a process could still
open the device and start streaming, which powered the chip up again
just before it was freed. fthd_start_streaming() now refuses with
-ENODEV once removing is set; removing is written under the same
vb2_queue_lock that vb2 holds around start_streaming.

isp_mem_create() returns NULL for a set file larger than its memory
region, and isp_load_set_file() dereferenced the result. Treat such a
file like a missing one and continue without calibration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 fthd_drv.c  | 6 ++++++
 fthd_isp.c  | 7 +++++++
 fthd_v4l2.c | 6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fthd_drv.c b/fthd_drv.c
index e5cb70c..83e0ee8 100644
--- a/fthd_drv.c
+++ b/fthd_drv.c
@@ -716,6 +716,12 @@ static void fthd_pci_remove(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 	fthd_power_restore(dev_priv);
 	mutex_unlock(&dev_priv->vb2_queue_lock);
 
+	/*
+	 * A firmware stop that timed out in the teardown queued a recovery;
+	 * it must not run once dev_priv is freed.
+	 */
+	cancel_work_sync(&dev_priv->recover_work);
+
 	fthd_v4l2_unregister(dev_priv);
 
 	pci_set_drvdata(pdev, NULL);
diff --git a/fthd_isp.c b/fthd_isp.c
index edc4a97..2008431 100644
--- a/fthd_isp.c
+++ b/fthd_isp.c
@@ -636,6 +636,13 @@ int fthd_isp_cmd_set_loadfile(struct fthd_private *dev_priv)
 		isp_free_set_file(dev_priv);
 
 	file = isp_mem_create(dev_priv, FTHD_MEM_SET_FILE, fw->size);
+	if (!file) {
+		dev_warn(&dev_priv->pdev->dev,
+			 "set file %s does not fit (%zu bytes), continuing without calibration\n",
+			 filename, fw->size);
+		release_firmware(fw);
+		return 0;
+	}
 	FTHD_S2_MEMCPY_TOIO(file->offset, fw->data, fw->size);
 
 	release_firmware(fw);
diff --git a/fthd_v4l2.c b/fthd_v4l2.c
index cd35f46..985905b 100644
--- a/fthd_v4l2.c
+++ b/fthd_v4l2.c
@@ -512,6 +512,12 @@ static int fthd_start_streaming(struct vb2_queue *vq, unsigned int count)
 	dev_priv->sequence = 0;
 	cancel_delayed_work(&dev_priv->idle_work);
 
+	/* remove tears the chip down and frees it; don't bring it up again */
+	if (dev_priv->removing) {
+		ret = -ENODEV;
+		goto fail;
+	}
+
 	/* A failed recovery or suspend left the chip down; try once more */
 	if (dev_priv->hw_state != FTHD_HW_UP) {
 		ret = fthd_hw_restart(dev_priv, true);
-- 
